# Extension Must Be Active: NONE
# Many important RISC-V extensions are currently active.
# Test Case Name: CSRRWI
# Test Case Type: INSTRUCTION
# Test Case Rule: RULE 1: CSRRWI obtains the XLEN-bit value to write to the CSR by zero-extending the 5-bit unsigned immediate field (uimm[4:0]) encoded in the rs1 field.
##### ASSEMBLY #####
csrrwi a0, mscratch, 26
# Result: mscratch = 26

# Extension Must Be Active: NONE
# Many important RISC-V extensions are currently active.
# Test Case Name: CSRRWI
# Test Case Type: INSTRUCTION
# Test Case Rule: RULE 2: If the destination register rd of a CSRRWI instruction is x0, the instruction shall not read the CSR and shall not cause any side effects that could occur on a CSR read.
##### ASSEMBLY #####
nop # Skipped because read side‑effects are not directly observable
# Result: x0 = 0

# Extension Must Be Active: NONE
# Many important RISC-V extensions are currently active.
# Test Case Name: CSRRWI
# Test Case Type: INSTRUCTION
# Test Case Rule: RULE 3: When rd of a CSRRWI instruction is x0, the instruction shall write the CSR with the zero-extended immediate value.
##### ASSEMBLY #####
csrrwi x0, mscratch, 7
# Result: mscratch = 7

# Extension Must Be Active: NONE
# Many important RISC-V extensions are currently active.
# Test Case Name: CSRRWI
# Test Case Type: INSTRUCTION
# Test Case Rule: RULE 4: When rd of a CSRRWI instruction is not x0, the instruction shall read the current value of the CSR, write the CSR with the zero-extended immediate value, and place the original CSR value into rd.
##### ASSEMBLY #####
li t0, 0x5
csrw mscratch, t0
csrrwi t1, mscratch, 3
# Result: t1 = 5

# Extension Must Be Active: D
# Many important RISC-V extensions are currently active.
# Test Case Name: FCVT.W.D
# Test Case Type: INSTRUCTION
# Test Case Rule: RULE 1: FCVT.W.D converts the double-precision floating-point value in floating-point register rs1 to a signed 32-bit integer and writes the result to integer register rd.
##### ASSEMBLY #####
li t0, 0x2a
fcvt.d.w ft0, t0, rne
fcvt.w.d a0, ft0, rne
# Result: a0 = 42

# Extension Must Be Active: D
# Many important RISC-V extensions are currently active.
# Test Case Name: FCVT.W.D
# Test Case Type: INSTRUCTION
# Test Case Rule: RULE 2: FCVT.W.D rounds the conversion result according to the rounding mode specified in the rm field of the instruction.
##### ASSEMBLY #####
li t0, 0x3ff8000000000000
fmv.d.x f1, t0
fcvt.w.d x5, f1, rtz
# Result: x5 = 1

# Extension Must Be Active: D
# Many important RISC-V extensions are currently active.
# Test Case Name: FCVT.W.D
# Test Case Type: INSTRUCTION
# Test Case Rule: RULE 4: FCVT.W.D must raise the floating-point exception flags that correspond to converting its double-precision source operand to a signed 32-bit integer, and the set of flags raised is identical to those that would be raised for FCVTMOD.W.D with the same operand.
##### ASSEMBLY #####
csrw fflags, x0
li t0, 0x7ff8000000000000
fmv.d.x f0, t0
fcvt.w.d a0, f0, rne
csrr t1, fflags
csrw fflags, x0
fcvtmod.w.d a1, f0, rne
csrr t2, fflags
xor t3, t1, t2
# Result: t3 = 0

