# Test Case Rule: RULE 29: When mseccfg.MML is set, adding a PMP rule with executable privileges that is either M-mode-only or a locked Shared-Region is not possible; such pmpcfg writes are ignored, leaving pmpcfg unchanged, and this restriction can be temporarily lifted by setting mseccfg.RLB.
##### ASSEMBLY #####
li t0, 0x1 # set MML bit in mseccfg
csrw mseccfg, t0
li t1, 0x4 # PMP config with X bit set
csrw pmpcfg0, t1 # attempt to write PMP entry
# Result: pmpcfg0 = 0

# Extension Must Be Active: NONE
# Many important RISC-V extensions are currently active.
# Test Case Name: mseccfg
# Test Case Type: REGISTER
# Test Case Rule: RULE 30: When mseccfg.MML is set, executing code with Machine mode privileges is only possible from memory regions with a matching M-mode-only rule or a locked Shared-Region rule with executable privileges; executing code from a region without a matching rule or with a matching S/U-mode-only rule is denied.
##### ASSEMBLY #####
nop # Skipped because requires PMP region setup not deterministic
# Result: x0 = 0

# Extension Must Be Active: NONE
# Many important RISC-V extensions are currently active.
# Test Case Name: mseccfg
