# Test Case Rule: RULE 36: Executing an xRET instruction (MRET or SRET) sets the mstatus field xIE to the value of xPIE, changes the current privilege mode to the value stored in xPP, sets xPIE in mstatus to 1, writes xPP in mstatus with the least-privileged supported mode (U if U-mode is implemented, otherwise M), and, if the saved privilege mode y is not M, also clears the MPRV bit in mstatus.
