# Test Case Rule: RULE 56: If MXLEN is 64 and S-mode is supported, the SXL field in the mstatus register is a WARL field that encodes the current SXLEN value.
##### ASSEMBLY #####
li t0, 0xc00000000
csrr t1, mstatus
and t2, t1, t0
srli t2, t2, 34
# Result: t2 = 2

# Extension Must Be Active: NONE
# Many important RISC-V extensions are currently active.
# Test Case Name: mstatus
# Test Case Type: REGISTER
# Test Case Rule: RULE 57: If MXLEN is 64 and U-mode is not supported, the UXL field in the mstatus register is read-only zero.
##### ASSEMBLY #####
nop # Skipped because U-mode is supported
# Result: x0 = 0

# Extension Must Be Active: NONE
# Many important RISC-V extensions are currently active.
# Test Case Name: mstatus
# Test Case Type: REGISTER
# Test Case Rule: RULE 58: If MXLEN is 64 and U-mode is supported, the UXL field in the mstatus register is a WARL field that encodes the current UXLEN value.
##### ASSEMBLY #####
csrr t0, mstatus
li t1, 0x300000000
and t2, t0, t1
# Result: t2 = 0x100000000

# Extension Must Be Active: NONE
# Many important RISC-V extensions are currently active.
# Test Case Name: mstatus
# Test Case Type: REGISTER
# Test Case Rule: RULE 59: When S-mode is implemented, the set of legal values for the UXL field in the mstatus register excludes any encoding that would cause UXLEN to be greater than SXLEN.
##### ASSEMBLY #####
li t1, 0x400000000 # Set SXL = 01 (SXLEN = 64)
csrw mstatus, t1
csrr t2, mstatus
li t0, 0x200000000 # Attempt to set UXL = 10 (UXLEN = 128) which is > SXLEN
or t2, t2, t0
csrw mstatus, t2
# Result: mcause = 2

# Extension Must Be Active: NONE
# Many important RISC-V extensions are currently active.
# Test Case Name: mstatus
# Test Case Type: REGISTER
# Test Case Rule: RULE 60: If the XLEN value for any privilege mode, as configured by the corresponding fields in the mstatus register, is less than the widest supported XLEN, then all operations must ignore source operand register bits above the configured XLEN and must sign-extend results to fill the entire widest supported XLEN in the destination register.
##### ASSEMBLY #####
nop # Skipped because configured XLEN equals widest XLEN
# Result: x0 = 0

# Extension Must Be Active: NONE
# Many important RISC-V extensions are currently active.
# Test Case Name: mstatus
# Test Case Type: REGISTER
# Test Case Rule: RULE 61: If the XLEN for a privilege mode, as defined by the mstatus register, is less than the widest supported XLEN, then PC bits above XLEN are ignored and any write to the PC is sign-extended to fill the widest supported XLEN.
##### ASSEMBLY #####
nop # Skipped because XLEN equals widest supported XLEN
# Result: x0 = 0

# Extension Must Be Active: NONE
# Many important RISC-V extensions are currently active.
# Test Case Name: mstatus
# Test Case Type: REGISTER
# Test Case Rule: RULE 62: The architecture imposes no checks that lower-privilege XLEN settings, as specified by the mstatus fields, are less than or equal to the XLEN setting of the next-higher privilege mode.
##### ASSEMBLY #####
li t0, 0x2
slli t0, t0, 33
csrw mstatus, t0
csrr t1, mstatus
li t2, 0x3
slli t2, t2, 33
and t3, t1, t2
# Result: t3 = 0x400000000

