# Test Case Rule: RULE 168: When a trap is taken into supervisor mode, the SPIE bit in mstatus is set to the value of the SIE bit in mstatus, and the SIE bit in mstatus is set to 0.
##### ASSEMBLY #####
nop # Skipped because trap entry CSR update not observable without custom handler
# Result: x0 = 0

# Extension Must Be Active: NONE
# Many important RISC-V extensions are currently active.
# Test Case Name: mstatus
# Test Case Type: REGISTER
# Test Case Rule: RULE 169: When an SRET instruction is executed, the SIE bit in mstatus is set to the value of the SPIE bit in mstatus, then the SPIE bit in mstatus is set to 1.
##### ASSEMBLY #####
li t1, 0x22 # mask for SPIE and SIE
csrc mstatus, t1 # clear SPIE and SIE (set both to 0)
call machine_to_supervisor # transition to S-mode
sret # execute SRET, should set SPIE=1, SIE=previous SPIE (0)
csrr a0, mstatus # read mstatus
li t2, 0x20 # mask for SPIE bit
and a0, a0, t2 # isolate SPIE
srli a0, a0, 5 # shift to LSB
# Result: a0 = 1

